"""Render review documents from reproducible evidence snapshots; no network or DB."""
import json
import pathlib
from collections import Counter
ROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
OUT=ROOT/'reports/source-expansion'
summary=json.loads((OUT/'summary.json').read_text())
inventory=json.loads((ROOT/'src/data/sources/research/inventory.json').read_text())
old=json.loads((OUT/'existing.json').read_text())
probes=json.loads((OUT/'probes.json').read_text())
reporters=json.loads((OUT/'reporters.json').read_text())
cost=json.loads((OUT/'cost-scenarios.json').read_text())
validation=json.loads((OUT/'validation.json').read_text()) if (OUT/'validation.json').exists() else {}
sources=inventory['sources'];by_id={s['id']:s for s in sources}
additions=[s for s in sources if not s['existingIds'] and s['qualified'] and s['type']!='X']
def table(headers,rows):
    clean=lambda x:str(x).replace('|','/').replace('\n',' ')
    return '| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |\n| '+' | '.join('---' for _ in headers)+' |\n'+''.join('| '+' | '.join(clean(x) for x in row)+' |\n' for row in rows)+'\n'
def write(name,text): (ROOT/name).write_text(text.rstrip()+"\n")
intro=f"Evidence captured {inventory['checkedAt']}. Isolated branch `poc/nfl-source-expansion`, base `5e1a6ec5`. Public publisher research and local tests only. No production/account/DB access, sends, deployment, paid services, or schedule changes. Production enablement, traffic, historical success, average volume and error rate are **UNKNOWN**.\n\n"
teamtable=table(['Team','Inventory','Qualified provisional','Technical RSS','Existing','New','Discovery only','Local X references','Qualified gap to 20'],[[t[k] for k in ('team','total','qualified','technicalFeeds','existing','new','discoveryOnly','localXReferences','qualifiedGap')] for t in summary['teams']])
audit='# NFL source audit\n\n'+intro+f"The repository contains **37 general**, **120 monitoring**, and **179 Film Room candidate records** (336 raw records). URL-backed identities normalize to {summary['existingUniqueSources']} existing sources; 171 video candidates and six general records lack URLs. These unresolved records remain in the CSV and original catalogs, but are excluded from URL-backed unique counts. Aliases are not deleted or rewritten.\n\n"
audit+='The general registry is `src/data/sources/index.ts` plus `src/server/source-registry.ts`. It previously comprised national/data sources and KC only. Monitoring (`src/data/sources/monitoring`) covers all 32 teams: 31 generated three-feed baselines, a richer KC catalog, and five shared national X reporters. Film Room (`src/data/sources/video/catalog.ts`) has 179 unresolved/review candidates, only eight with candidate URLs. Its immutable channel-ID resolution is a separate requirement. The legacy migration 012 also seeds three source records; these are migration seeds, not evidence of deployed rows.\n\n'
audit+='`observer.ts` syncs monitoring into PostgreSQL `content_sources`; only active, LIVE RSS records become enabled. X, public pages and Reddit are not dispatched by that path. LIVE is derived from configuration/environment presence, not a health test. The 97 configured RSS sources have nominal intervals totaling 18,504 checks/day. The current eight-run global scheduler calls `scheduleDueSources` with batch size 10, allowing at most 80 newly scheduled fetch jobs/day before video competition, retries and existing backlog. A 50-job drain/run and generation caps also constrain throughput. Do not confuse the nominal intervals with measured polling or freshness.\n\n'
audit+='RSS/Atom uses `RssSourceFetcher`; ETag/Last-Modified and exponential failure backoff already exist. YouTube uses resolved uploads playlists via `playlistItems.list`, not keyword search. No free X ingestion is demonstrated. There is no production D1/R2 binding in this branch: the configured Cloudflare Worker is an authenticated scheduler calling the Next.js/PostgreSQL API. No KV or Cloudflare Queues is configured here; PostgreSQL ingestion jobs are the queue. External data providers include ESPN, OverTheCap, Spotrac and Pro Football Reference, but their presence does not establish an authorized news API contract.\n\n'
audit+='Candidates normalize titles, links, hashes and team associations. Uniqueness is `(source_id, external_id)` / `(source_id, canonical_url)`, preserving separate attribution; fingerprints are indexed but not globally unique. Same-event clustering attaches evidence to saved story IDs and material changes produce revisions. Canonical projections feed The Beat, team homepages, Three & Out and Catch Up. Video candidates remain isolated for Film Room. Daily delivery currently implements push; email/SMS preferences do not prove delivery adapters exist. Existing synthesis must not be treated as an independent fact checker.\n\n'
audit+=f"Public check observations: **{len(probes)} requests**, **{sum(p.get('status')==200 for p in probes)} HTTP 200**, **{sum('feedItems' in p for p in probes)} parsed feed responses** (multiple advertised section/feed URLs can belong to one source), **{summary['technicalFeedSources']} unique source identities with a recent nonempty feed**. Feed freshness requires at least one non-future item within 45 days. Future-dated entries are excluded from the freshness signal. A single snapshot cannot establish a daily average or historical error rate. 403/402 results were retained without bypass attempts. No full article bodies are retained in research artifacts.\n\n"
audit+='The following inventory shows configured state, not enabled production state. Last ingestion success, average daily items, and historical error rates are UNKNOWN for every row. The linked CSV and `existing.json` contain all source URLs, original IDs and associations.\n\n'
audit+=table(['Catalog','Source ID','Name','Team/scope','Method/platform','Configured status','Local observation'],[[catalog,s['id'],s.get('displayName',s['name']),s.get('teamId',s.get('team')) or 'NFL/shared',s.get('ingestionMethod',s.get('platform',s.get('category'))),'active flag' if s.get('active',s.get('enabled')) else s.get('status','disabled/review'),next((p.get('error') or ('RSS parsed' if 'feedItems' in p else 'HTTP '+str(p.get('status'))) for p in probes if p['url']==(s.get('rssUrl') or s.get('metadata',{}).get('feedUrl') or s.get('canonicalUrl') or s.get('url') or s.get('candidateUrl'))),'not probed / URL unresolved')] for catalog,ss in old.items() for s in ss])
audit+='Original reporting is not established by catalog trust scores. Official feeds provide first-party announcements; aggregator aliases require original-publisher tracing. See per-source assessments and provisional evidence components in `inventory.json`. No existing source was removed.\n'
write('NFL_SOURCE_AUDIT.md',audit)
write('EXISTING_SOURCE_AUDIT.md','# Existing source audit\n\nThe complete audit is [NFL_SOURCE_AUDIT.md](NFL_SOURCE_AUDIT.md), including every pre-change catalog record.\n')
research='# NFL source research\n\n'+intro+f"**The 20-qualified-per-team / 640-qualified-assignment objective is NOT met.** There are {summary['uniqueSources']} URL-backed source identities, {summary['teamAssignments']} raw team assignments, {summary['qualifiedUniqueSources']} provisionally qualified unique candidates and {sum(t['qualified'] for t in summary['teams'])} qualified team assignments. Raw assignment totals include shared national references; they are not qualified coverage. All 32 teams have documented gaps.\n\n"
research+='Discovery started with [Sharp Sources](https://sharpsources.com/sources), its [newsletter directory](https://sharpsources.com/newsletters/), [PFWA contacts](https://www.profootballwriters.org/about-the-pfwa/pfwa-contacts/), and [Unabated](https://www.unabated.com/post/best-nfl-twitter-follows). All 32 public team discovery pages were read, then primary publisher pages and their advertised feed links were checked directly. Additional independent sources were checked in `manual-candidates.json`. Directory inclusion alone never qualifies a source. PFWA corroborates chapter roles, not ingestion rights or current X activity. Older media guides/search results were not used to assert current affiliation.\n\n'
research+='Scoring is provisional and conservative: original reporting 0–25, reliability 0–25, team relevance 0–20, freshness 0–15, uniqueness 0–10, technical access 0–5. A current official feed earns 20/20/20/15/5/5 = 85; this is first-party announcement authority, not independent scrutiny. For other publications, a byline earns only 5 originality points; a named primary byline 10 accountability points within reliability (accuracy still unreviewed); associated team 20; recent primary metadata/feed 15; distinct non-aggregator identity 5; working feed 5 (page only 3). Thus a signed recent non-aggregator with a feed can reach 60 (Tier 3), not Tier 1. Aggregators receive no originality/uniqueness credit. Unknown evidence earns zero. A byline is weak evidence of authored content, not proof of original reporting or audited accuracy. Quality tier is separate from production trust/confidence and legal eligibility. These provisional qualifications require editorial review before production.\n\n'
research+='Feed verification means a public nonempty RSS/Atom response with recent dated items. It does not grant permission to republish a description, encoded article body, transcript or image. All rights statuses remain REVIEW_REQUIRED and all automated eligibility is false; Technically fetchable identities are reported separately below. Public-page extraction, newsletter subscription, YouTube API access, or X access is not enabled automatically.\n\n'+teamtable
for t in summary['teams']:
    ss=[by_id[l['sourceId']] for l in inventory['teamSources'] if l['teamId']==t['team']]
    research+='## '+t['team']+'\n\n'+table(['Source','Primary URL','Type','Score / tier','Verification','Qualified'],[[s['name'],f"[{s['canonicalDomain']}]({s['sampleUrls'][-1]})",s['type'],f"{s['qualityScore']} / {s['tier'] or 'review'}",s['verificationStatus'],s['qualified']] for s in ss])
research+='## Reporter research limitations\n\n'+f"{len(reporters)} exact account URLs were recovered from the supplied directory. None is ingested. Each record in `reporters.json` includes name, handle, team, directory affiliation, specialty, activity (UNKNOWN), reliability (unestablished), ingestion feasibility and equivalent authorized URL (not yet resolved). Five qualified local X accounts per team are NOT demonstrated; the team table gives actual reference counts. A directory label points to a different handle in the Atlanta entry; it is flagged DIRECTORY_CONFLICT. Directory affiliations may have changed. Do not convert these references into trusted automated reporting or duplicate the same reporter via multiple profile paths. Primary biography verification and five-current-account coverage remain explicit research blockers.\n\n"
research+='Coverage still needs more original local reporting, independently reviewed film/cap specialists and resolved podcasts per team. Category quotas were not filled with anonymous channels, outdated accounts or repeated national feeds. The initial named starter publications were compared against monitoring profiles, direct discovery and manual checks. Missing direct verification remains a gap; it is not evidence that an outlet has closed.\n'
write('NFL_SOURCE_RESEARCH.md',research)
comparison='# NFL source comparison\n\n'+intro+teamtable+'Existing/New counts are URL-backed identities within each team, not additive totals across teams. Shared nationals are stored once. Configured active, configured inactive, one-shot failing, new provisional candidate and new discovery-only classifications are in `inventory.json`; none claims current production health. Existing functioning sources remain unchanged. Aliases group homepage/feed variants and exact social profiles; they do not merge two reporters merely because both use X or two newsletters because both use Substack. NBC editorial desks retain explicit path identities. Unresolved URLs/IDs stay unresolved.\n\n'
comparison+='## Existing alias groups\n\n'+table(['Source','Existing IDs preserved','Action'],[[s['name'],', '.join(s['existingIds']),'DUPLICATE research alias; preserve original IDs and history'] for s in sources if len(s['existingIds'])>1])
comparison+='## New locally registered disabled candidates\n\n'+table(['Source ID','Source','Technical feed','Action'],[[s['id'],s['name'],s['canonicalFeedUrl'] or 'none','NEW_RECOMMENDED, disabled pending rights/quality/cost review'] for s in additions])
write('NFL_SOURCE_COMPARISON.md',comparison)
costdoc='# NFL source cost analysis\n\n'+intro+'**Added live infrastructure cost is $0 because new ingestion remains disabled. A whole-product $0 launch is NOT certified.** Current account quotas, billing plan and usage cannot be determined from source code and were not accessed. Current traffic is UNKNOWN. Scenario DAU and content volume are explicit assumptions, not analytics.\n\n'
costdoc+='Published reference allowances are account-wide: Workers Free 100,000 requests/day and 10 ms CPU/invocation; D1 5 million rows read and 100,000 written/day including indexes, 500 MB/database and 5 GB/account. Additional databases do not add daily write allowance. [Worker limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/), [D1 limits](https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/limits/), [D1 pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/pricing/). R2 Standard includes 10 GB-month, 1 million Class A and 10 million Class B operations/month; these are allowances, not a hard spending cap. [R2 pricing](https://developers.cloudflare.com/r2/pricing/). No KV/Queues were added; their unused allowances do not subsidize D1 writes.\n\n'
costdoc+='The main branch has PostgreSQL ingestion, not the D1 POC. Local commit `074f0e60` measured 474.18 MB standard / 535.87 MB entropy after conditional archival cleanup, both above the 350 MB target. Subsequent isolated commit `ae40533f` modeled lean D1/R2 at 321.16 MB D1 and 6,025.14 MB R2 at 365 days with 67,709 writes/day. That separate experiment did not certify production CPU, current accounts, live source throughput or complete $0 hosting. Its baseline is a conditional sensitivity reference here, not a merged architecture or a new benchmark result.\n\n'
costdoc+='The model uses 200 baseline unique candidates/day, 1,040 checks/day, 1,400 terminal jobs/day and the prior local measurements of 30.26 writes/candidate, 10.03/check and 26/job. Additional checks/candidates each conservatively add a job. Incremental retained D1 estimates are 2,048 bytes/candidate, 256/check and 192/job, including a planning allowance for metadata/index/receipt storage; these are assumptions requiring measured page audits on the final architecture. R2 adds two immutable 8 KiB payload copies/candidate plus eight D1 backup copies. Raw copyrighted bodies are not assumed ingestible. Higher entropy/worst-case 512,000-byte original payloads must be budgeted separately; each extra 200/day at that ceiling would add 74.75 GB/year for two copies before backups, exceeding R2 Free.\n\n'
costdoc+=f"There are {summary['technicalFeedSources']} unique feed-capable source identities. An **evaluation-only** eight-checks/feed/day ceiling would require {summary['technicalFeedSources']*8:,} feed requests/day; existing global batch scheduling supports at most 80 new fetch jobs/day. This model does not change cron or assert that throughput is delivered. Unknown measured daily volume yields no adaptive interval recommendation. More source diversity should replace redundant fetches/content, not imply linear unbounded new candidates. A seven-day, explicitly authorized health observation is needed before setting per-source adaptive cadence. Conditional requests reduce transfer/parsing; they still consume HTTP requests, checks and scheduling/health writes.\n\n"
costdoc+=table(['Scenario','Assumed DAU','Unique candidates/day','Feed requests/day','Worker requests/day','D1 reads/day','D1 writes/day','D1 MB 365','R2 MB 365','R2 A/month','R2 B/month','Monthly cost'],[[s['label'],s['dau'],s['uniqueCandidatesPerDay'],s['feedRequestsPerDay'],s['workerRequestsPerDay'],s['d1ReadsPerDay'],s['d1WritesPerDay'],round(s['d1Mb']['365'],2),round(s['r2Mb365'],2),s['r2ClassAMonth'],s['r2ClassBMonth'],'Unknown / not Free-feasible' if s['projectedMonthlyCostUsd'] is None else '$0 conditional'] for s in cost])
costdoc+=table(['Scenario','30d D1 MB','90d D1 MB','180d D1 MB','365d D1 MB','First blocker'],[[s['label']]+[round(s['d1Mb'][str(d)],2) for d in (30,90,180,365)]+['350 MB engineering target before year end' if s['label']=='current-reference-only' else '500 MB D1 storage before year end' if s['label']=='launch' else 'D1 daily writes from day one' if s['label']=='2x-launch' else 'Worker requests and D1 daily writes from day one'] for s in cost])
costdoc+='The zero-DAU reference is NOT current traffic/usage: its enlarged feed workload still exceeds the engineering storage target. Current-traffic first limit is UNKNOWN. At launch D1 storage fails; at 2× launch D1 writes fail immediately and R2 storage later; at 5× launch requests and writes fail immediately, and R2 storage/Class B also fail. No paid overage is activated or quoted as an acceptable fallback. Formulae and all scenario inputs are in `cost-model.ts` and `cost-scenarios.json`. Traffic assumptions affect API reads/requests; source volume is explicitly varied separately rather than assuming users themselves create news.\n\n'
costdoc+='Worker CPU is UNMEASURED. Local parse timing is Node wall time and cannot establish a Cloudflare 10 ms CPU pass. See `reports/source-expansion/local-benchmark.json` for typical, large and near-1-MiB feed parse/normalize/hash timings; no network, database or deployed Worker CPU was measured. Neither a 60-second Next route timeout nor cron wall time changes that CPU limit. Existing scheduler only performs the forwarding request; source parsing occurs on the Next/PostgreSQL host. Existing Next SSR/native Argon2, PostgreSQL hosting/wakeups, email delivery and AI hosting still require provider-specific budgets. Five-minute Three & Out database polling can prevent free PostgreSQL suspension; the prior Neon example (0.25 CU continuously = 180 CU-hours/month) exceeded its 100 CU-hour Free allowance. [Neon pricing](https://neon.com/pricing).\n\n'
costdoc+='New external API usage is zero. X API access is not assumed free, and X references are DISCOVERY_ONLY. [X API pricing](https://docs.x.com/x-api/getting-started/pricing). Existing YouTube playlist polling costs quota per request; account project quota/credentials are unverified, and unresolved channel handles remain held. [YouTube quota costs](https://developers.google.com/youtube/data/determine_quota_cost). Paid search/news/AI dependencies were not introduced.\n'
write('NFL_SOURCE_COST_ANALYSIS.md',costdoc)
gates={'minimumQualifiedPerTeam':all(t['qualified']>=20 for t in summary['teams']),'minimumQualifiedAssignments':sum(t['qualified'] for t in summary['teams'])>=640,'fiveLocalXReferencesPerTeam':all(t['localXReferences']>=5 for t in summary['teams']),'rightsApprovedNewSources':False,'productionFreeTierCertified':False,'newIngestionEnabled':False,'teams':summary['teams']}
(OUT/'release-gates.json').write_text(json.dumps(gates,indent=2)+'\n')
results='# NFL source implementation results\n\n'+intro+f"Status: **HOLD — source coverage and production free-tier gates fail.** {summary['uniqueSources']} unique URL-backed identities, {summary['teamAssignments']} raw assignments, {summary['qualifiedUniqueSources']} provisional candidates / {sum(t['qualified'] for t in summary['teams'])} qualified assignments. {len(additions)} qualified new publication records enter the general registry locally, all disabled. {summary['newUniqueSources']} total new identities include held discovery references. {summary['technicalFeedSources']} source identities have technically verified feeds; **zero newly approved automated-ingestion-eligible sources**, **zero new enabled production sources**. Existing production enabled count is UNKNOWN.\n\n"
results+='Changes: normalized research inventory and explicit source/team links, preserved existing ID aliases, bounded evidence quality scores separate from publishing confidence, normalized shared-feed/adaptive planning helpers (planning only), and disabled additions through the existing general registry. No migration is necessary: research relationships live in the versioned catalog; existing PostgreSQL metadata/health columns are retained. Recovery is to revert the commit/disable the new additions; no stored editorial data, IDs or source rows were deleted or backfilled. There is no automatic database migration or source activation script.\n\n'
results+='Existing pipeline improvements: source sync now skips identical PostgreSQL updates; RSS fetching validates each redirect before contacting its target and caps response bytes at 1 MiB; invalid feed envelopes, unsafe item links and malformed item dates do not become successful candidates; conditional requests/timeout/failure backoff remain. Same-host publication aliases no longer count as independent corroboration. Exact substantial syndicated copy can match one canonical story while preserving separate evidence. Headline-only evidence is held for review and cannot be synthesized into factual claims. No inference of original reporting is made from publication popularity; selecting original reporters still requires item-level attribution review. The full existing feed description/encoded-content storage path remains a production blocker for publisher rights and size policy; the new registry does not enable it for new sources.\n\n'
results+=f"Tests: **{validation.get('unitTestsPassed', 'See logs')} unit/source-contract tests passed; {validation.get('unitTestsFailed', 'see logs')} failed. One disposable PostgreSQL mutation check passed. Typecheck, formatting and diff checks passed.** "
results+='See `reports/source-expansion/tests.txt`, `typecheck.txt` and `validation.json` for final counts and commands. Existing stale assertions about retired GitHub cron schedules, a missing group argument and the replaced inline NewsGraphic component failed unchanged on the base checkout; `baseline-test-failures.txt` records this. Only those test expectations were updated to the current manual backup/isolated queue contract; cron/workflow runtime files were not changed. The minimum-20 test records actual gaps; a passing unit suite does NOT pass the editorial release gate. No Android/iOS/browser UI validation was required or performed; no product screens changed.\n\n'
results+='Remaining work: complete 20 independently reviewed quality sources and five current local reporter references per team; verify primary bylines, original reporting, corrections/reliability, recent activity and equivalent authorized reporter feeds; resolve immutable YouTube IDs; review source-specific reuse terms; measure seven-day volume/duplicate ratio and backlog latency; demonstrate a bounded end-to-end fetch/queue budget and publication/source-ID mapping on the selected storage architecture; run account/production CPU/quota checks only under separate authorization. Saved story links, historical search, attribution, corrections, Three & Out/Film Room relationships and rollback need integrated rehearsal before cutover; no production integration is claimed here.\n\n'
results+='Recommended rollout: keep additions disabled. Review the inventory and failed release gates, select a small mix of original local reporting and film sources, approve metadata/excerpt use per publisher, then validate read/write/storage/CPU throughput in an isolated rehearsal with original IDs. Require measured headroom and working historical/source attribution resolution before any enablement. Stop for review; do not deploy.\n\n'
results+='Deliverables: `NFL_SOURCE_AUDIT.md`, `EXISTING_SOURCE_AUDIT.md`, `NFL_SOURCE_RESEARCH.md`, `NFL_SOURCE_COMPARISON.md`, `NFL_SOURCE_REGISTRY.csv`, `NFL_SOURCE_COST_ANALYSIS.md`, this report; machine-readable snapshots, costs, gaps and validations under `reports/source-expansion`; runtime additions/policy under `src/data/sources/research`; feed/editorial improvements under the existing story engine. No Front Office or Parlay Lab code was changed. A complete changed-file manifest is in `reports/source-expansion/changed-files.txt`. The inherited deterministic fallback also contains Kansas City-specific headline templates and monitoring sync maps official sources to LOCAL_OUTLET; those all-team publishing semantics need correction/rehearsal before rollout. New sources remain gated.\n'
write('NFL_SOURCE_IMPLEMENTATION_RESULTS.md',results)
print('Reports written; failed release gates remain explicit.')
